    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hi, it’s good to meet you. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S011",
      "patient_response": "Nice to meet you too. So, um, what brings me in is... well, I keep getting up when I'm supposed to just stay put. Like, I'll be right in the middle of a client interview—I'm a private investigator, mostly doing background checks and surveillance, which, let me tell you, involves a lot of sitting in cars. I had this one case last month where I was parked outside a diner for six hours straight, just waiting for this guy to show up. He never did, turns out he was in Florida the whole time, completely blew my weekend. \n\nBut anyway, yeah, during client interviews, or when I'm doing these tutoring sessions I volunteer for, or even just sitting at my book club, I just can't seem to stay in my chair. People are really starting to notice that I can't just sit and listen. Like at book club last Tuesday, we were reading this historical fiction thing—way too long, honestly, the author spent three pages describing a dress, I ended up skimming half of it—and my friend Susan actually stopped mid-sentence to ask if I had a bad back or something because I kept standing up and pacing around her living room while she was trying to talk.",
