    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you get up and pace, is it because you feel driven to do it to relieve a distressing thought or urge that keeps intruding on you?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, it's not like that at all. I don't have any, like, weird thoughts or anything forcing me to do it. It's just... my body feels like it has to move. Like a motor running, you know? Speaking of motors, my car has been making this awful rattling sound lately. I took it to the mechanic on Elm Street—the one with the big neon sign, you know it? He said it was the catalytic converter, but I swear he's trying to overcharge me. I mean, five hundred dollars just for the part? That's ridiculous. I should probably get a second opinion. My cousin's husband is pretty good with cars, maybe I'll ask him this weekend at the family barbecue. We're having ribs. But yeah, no distressing thoughts or whatever you said. Just can't stay seated.",
