    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do you spend a lot of time worrying about many different things, even when there isn’t a clear reason to?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, not really. I mean, I don't just sit around worrying for no reason. I worry about normal things, I guess, like if I'm going to finish a background check on time, or... oh, like my landlord just raised the rent again, which is so annoying because he just painted the outside of the building this absolutely hideous mustard yellow color. I have no idea who picked it out. Probably his wife, honestly, she has terrible taste. \n\nI saw her at the grocery store last week buying, like, six whole cantaloupes. Who needs six cantaloupes at once? Unless you're making a massive fruit salad, but even then, cantaloupe is always the filler fruit that nobody actually wants to eat, you know? Everyone always picks around it to get to the strawberries first. I actually tried growing strawberries on my balcony last summer, but the birds kept getting to them before I could. I bought this little plastic owl to scare them away, but it completely fell over in the wind and just laid there for a month. \n\nBut, um... wait, what were you asking? Oh, right, worrying. Yeah, no, I don't really do that. I just deal with things as they happen.",
