    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often blurt out answers or interrupt people before they’ve finished speaking?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S018",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, I guess I do that a lot. Like, if I hear the junior detectives at the agency discussing a lead, I'll just jump right in with questions or advice before I've even been asked. Speaking of the junior guys, one of them—Jason, I think his name is?—he makes the absolute worst coffee. It’s basically just hot brown water. I actually had to bring in my own French press last week because I couldn't take it anymore, but cleaning the coffee grounds out of those things is such a hassle. They get everywhere, and my plumber said I'm going to completely ruin my sink pipes if I keep washing them down the drain. He charges a fortune, by the way, just to come out and look at a pipe. \n\nBut, um... oh, right. Yeah, it's not just at work, either. If I hear a neighbor talking in the hallway, I do the exact same thing. I just start talking. It's only afterward that I realize I completely barged into someone else's conversation. Like my neighbor Mrs. Gable, she was talking to the mailman about her rhododendrons, and I just interrupted to give her fertilizer tips. I don't even garden! Well, except for those doomed strawberries I told you about. But yeah, I definitely jump in before people are done talking.",
