    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often get into arguments with people in authority, like supervisors, teachers, or police?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Arguments with authority? Um, no, not really. I mean, I don't go looking for fights with my boss or anything. My boss is actually pretty laid back, mostly because he spends half the day playing solitaire on his computer. I saw his screen once when I walked in to drop off a file—it was that old version with the cascading cards when you win, you know? It's so retro. It reminds me of the first computer I ever bought back in the nineties. It was this massive beige block, and the dial-up sound was so loud it would wake up my cat. \n\nMy cat's name was Barnaby, by the way. He was this huge orange tabby who used to sleep right on top of the warm monitor. You can't do that with flat screens anymore, which is probably a bummer for modern cats. I wonder where they sleep now? Probably on keyboards. I saw a video online the other day of a cat that actually typed out an email to its owner's boss just by walking across the desk. It was just a bunch of gibberish, but still, pretty funny. \n\nAnyway, what was the question? Oh, arguing. Yeah, no, I don't really argue with cops or bosses or anything. I just do my job and try to get out of there.",
